From ba626e4a59bc07f3461a4b079f415d3baa8dc454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Bestmann <oliver.bestmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:48:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backends/drm: report damage to the kernel with
 FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS

Backport of the commit of the same name on master to 6.7.5.

So far the property was always set to 0, which tells the driver that the
whole buffer changed. Each layer now records what changed in every frame
it produces, and a commit sets the clips to everything that changed since
the last frame that's known to have reached the screen. Frames that are
still queued are counted as not presented, so dropped or merged commits
can't lead to too little damage being reported.

Damage isn't known for direct scanout, test buffers and rotated outputs;
those keep reporting the whole buffer.
